Hi Killan,

Yes increasing X until you find that there are no more changes in growth predictions is showing you when feeding has become ad libitum and is limited by 'handling', not by encounter rate.

Re estimating the feeding parameters including K, have a read of:

van der Meer, J. (2006) An introduction to Dynamic Energy Budget (DEB) models with special emphasis on parameter estimation. Journal of Sea Research, 56, 85–102.

All the best,
Mike

